Code
----

androidtvremote2 (https://github.com/tronikos/androidtvremote2)
  Apache License 2.0. The Android TV Remote protocol client in
  firmware/remote/components/atv_remote is a C port of it, and its key codes
  (atv_keycodes.h) and the self-test's golden vectors (atv_golden.h) are
  generated from its remotemessage.proto and polo.proto, vendored in
  firmware/remote/components/atv_remote/proto with its LICENSE. Those protos
  come in turn from androidtv-remote (https://github.com/louis49/androidtv-remote,
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2021 louis49; its license text is
  proto/LICENSE-androidtv-remote) and from AOSP's
  google-tv-pairing-protocol (Copyright 2009 Google Inc., Apache License
  2.0), as their header comments say.

ESP-IDF (https://github.com/espressif/esp-idf)
  Apache License 2.0. The firmware is built on it and links its components,
  which carry their own licenses (FreeRTOS: MIT; lwIP: BSD-3-Clause;
  Mbed TLS: Apache-2.0; cJSON: MIT; and others listed in ESP-IDF).

Espressif components from the ESP Component Registry, fetched at build time
  esp_lvgl_port, esp_lcd_touch, esp_lcd_touch_gt911, mdns: Apache License
  2.0.

LVGL (https://lvgl.io)
  MIT License. Copyright (c) LVGL Kft. Its built-in Montserrat 14 font
  (SIL Open Font License 1.1, with Font Awesome symbols) is compiled in as
  LVGL's default font.

esp_littlefs (https://github.com/joltwallet/esp_littlefs)
  MIT License. Copyright 2020 Brian Pugh. It contains littlefs
  (https://github.com/littlefs-project/littlefs), BSD-3-Clause, Copyright
  (c) 2022 The littlefs authors and (c) 2017 Arm Limited.

ESP Web Tools (https://github.com/esphome/esp-web-tools)
  Apache License 2.0. Vendored in firmware/remote/web/esp-web-tools, with
  its LICENSE, and changed in one place (a failed install offers Close
  instead of Back; see VERSION there). Its bundle includes Material Web
  (Apache License 2.0), lit (BSD-3-Clause), esptool-js with Espressif's
  flasher stubs (Apache License 2.0), improv-wifi-serial-sdk (Apache
  License 2.0), pako (MIT and Zlib), atob-lite (MIT) and tslib (0BSD).

